From: Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Retry firmware readiness per PMIC GLINK service generation

Retry transient notification subscription and synchronous UCSI registration
failures at one-second intervals, at most ten attempts per service instance.
Do not consume a new service's retry budget with an old request, or postpone
its UP event with a stale delayed retry. Coalesced DOWN/UP must replace old
UCSI ports even when the worker only sees the final UP state.

Drain battery work before releasing its client on removal and probe unwind.
Serialize UCSI connector notification dispatch with registration ownership,
while preserving command completions needed to finish pending transactions.
Reset the reused core's initialization budget and pending-event bit; publish
ports only after the final CCI read succeeds so retries clean up partial ports.

OEM reference (no automatic retry in these public implementations):
https://github.com/MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource/blob/eb49e10028e27fa98856cb5e458c0f0ec5b4554e/drivers/power/supply/qti_battery_charger.c
https://github.com/MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource/blob/eb49e10028e27fa98856cb5e458c0f0ec5b4554e/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c
Built on the registration ownership fix already carried in patch 0042:
https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8450-liuqin/commit/9f9cd5ac3bc1fade2c2584a051913a2b03d506d2
Retry budgets and generation tracking are local Linux recovery policy.
No firmware restart, PPM reset override or charging-policy write is added.

